{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Observe for yourself what I command you today.</b> He did not say regarding all the commandments that had already passed <b>'I command you.'</b> Therefore we must explain that he is saying: observe the commandments that I command you today, and do not do with them as you did with what I commanded you at first, for you transgressed everything to serve idolatry. And He promised to drive out the nations and warned against their idolatry and against their covenants, just as He did in the passage 'Behold, I send an angel before you' (above, 23:20–33), so that they would return to the original conditions. And He added here (Exodus 34:17), 'You shall not make for yourself molten gods,' that they should not do as they did with the calf, even with the intention of heaven to make it a guide before them. And He restored the matter of the three pilgrimage festivals, to see in them the face of the master, YHWH, the Elohim of Israel (Exodus 34:23), just as He did there, and the reason is known, for it comes after the warning against idolatry, and I have already explained it at the end of 'Jethro heard' (Ramban on Exodus 20:22)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:19:37.598712434Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}